s.\n\nWe need to evaluate criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's see each candidate:\n\nA: strong technical (anticipate dangerous, complex connections, spatial vision), leadership, but concerns: unorganized, not good at criticism (adaptability), maybe reliability? Not mentioned. No stress resilience evidence. Cooperation? Not mentioned.\n\nB: conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good weather assessment (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), but grumpy, uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). No decision quality evidence.\n\nC: 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere (crew cooperation), can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), but difficulty communicating ideas (communication), egocentric (cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). Good reliability, decision, but communication issues.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), concentration, problem solving (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but arrogant (crew cooperation), weak leadership (leadership). No reliability evidence.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? C seems strong on reliability, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be concerning for cockpit. B has stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative. D has problem solving and responsibility but arrogance. A has technical but organization and criticism issues.\n\nProbably C is strongest overall, but need to address communication concerns. Could ask other panel members for more info on C's communication. But we need to make a first contribution. We can propose C as provisional recommendation, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns, and ask for clarification on communication.\n\nThus public message: I recommend Candidate C, because reliability 100%, correct